{"cuisine/bolivian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/bolivian-cuisine","n":"Bolivian cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Bolivia","intro":[["Bolivian cuisine is the indigenous cuisine of Bolivia from the Aymara and Inca cuisine traditions, among other Andean and Amazonian groups. Later influences stemmed from Spaniards, Germans, Italians, French, and Arabs Asians due to the arrival of conquistadors and immigrants from those countries. The  traditional staples of Bolivian cuisine are corn, potatoes, quinoa and beans. These ingredients have been combined with a number of staples brought by the Spanish, such as rice, wheat, beef, and pork."],["Bolivian cuisine differs by geographical locations. In Western Bolivia in the Altiplano, due to the high, cold climate, cuisine tends to use spices, whereas in the lowlands of Bolivia in the more Amazonian regions, dishes consist of products abundant in the region: fruits, vegetables, fish and yuca."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"bolivian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolivian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Chipa by the Dozen","ref":"site/chipabythedozen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"chipabythedozen.com","note":"Bolivian-American Lizet Bowen's bilingual blog of Bolivian recipes.","url":"https://chipabythedozen.com/en/category/bolivian-food-recipes-savory-sweet/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":5,"links":[["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Chola sandwich","dish/chola-sandwich"],["Coca tea","dish/coca-tea"],["Locro","dish/locro"],["Salteña","dish/saltena"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Capsicum chinense","ingredient/capsicum-chinense"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Escabeche","ingredient/escabeche"],["Pernil","ingredient/pernil"],["Torresmo","ingredient/torresmo"],["Coca leaf","ingredient/coca-leaf"],["Beef jerky","ingredient/beef-jerky"],["Cayenne pepper","ingredient/cayenne-pepper"],["Chorizo","ingredient/chorizo"],["Hot sauce","ingredient/hot-sauce"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Zapallo","ingredient/zapallo"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Gelatin","ingredient/gelatin"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"More from Bolivia","count":1,"links":[["Aymara foodways","cuisine/aymara-foodways"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/17/Horneados_de_Santa_Cruz_.jpg/500px-Horneados_de_Santa_Cruz_.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Wawitasny","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horneados_de_Santa_Cruz_.jpg"}},"cuisine/jordanian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/jordanian-cuisine","n":"Jordanian cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Jordan","intro":[["Jordanian cuisine is a Levantine cuisine developed over time in Jordan. Stuffed vegetables are common, with many different techniques employed in their preparation.  Meat is an important component of Jordanian cuisine, most often lamb, beef and chicken but also goat and camel meat. Rice is frequently served as a side dish but there are also one-pot rice dishes such as maqloubah."],["As one of the largest producers of olives in the world, olive oil is the main cooking oil by Jordanians and Jordan as a whole. Herbs, garlic, onion, tomato sauce, and lemon are typical flavors found in Jordan."],["The blend of spices called za'atar contains a common local herb called sumac that grows wild in Jordan and is closely identified with Jordanian and other Middle Eastern countries."],["Yogurt is commonly served alongside food and is a common ingredient itself; in particular, jameed, a form of dried yogurt is unique to Jordanian cuisine and a main ingredient in mansaf, the national dish of Jordan, and a symbol in Jordanian culture for generosity."],["Another famous meat dish in Jordan is zarb. It is especially popular in areas inhabited by Bedouin tribes such as Petra and the desert of Wadi Rum where it is commonly served to tourists. Zarb is prepared in a submerged oven called a taboon, and is considered a delicacy. It consists of a selection of meat (usually chicken and lamb), vegetables (zucchini, eggplant, carrots, potatoes) and is served with rice and various meze, such as tabbouleh salad."],["Internationally known foods which are common and popular everyday snacks in Jordan include hummus, which is a purée of chick peas blended with tahini, lemon, and garlic, and falafel, a deep-fried ball or patty made from ground chickpeas."],["A typical mezze includes foods such as kibbeh, labaneh, baba ghanoush, tabbouleh, olives and pickles. Bread, rice, freekeh and bulgur all have a role in Jordanian cuisine."],["Popular desserts include baklava, knafeh, halva and qatayef (a dish made specially for Ramadan), in addition to seasonal fruits such as watermelons, figs, and cactus pear which are served in summer."],["Turkish coffee and tea flavored with mint or sage are almost ubiquitous in Jordan. Arabic coffee is also usually served on more formal occasions."],["Arak, an aniseed flavoured spirit is also drunk with food."],["Pork consumption in Jordan is negligible, with very modest amounts consumed per capita."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"jordanian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordanian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Dishes","count":4,"links":[["Qalayet bandora","dish/qalayet-bandora"],["Qatayef","dish/qatayef"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"],["Taboon bread","dish/taboon-bread"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Baking powder","ingredient/baking-powder"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Pistachio nut","ingredient/pistachio-nut"],["Semolina","ingredient/semolina"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Zucchini","ingredient/zucchini"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f3/Ajlun_Breakfast.jpg/500px-Ajlun_Breakfast.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Smart Viral at English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajlun_Breakfast.jpg"}},"dish/bacon-and-cabbage":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bacon-and-cabbage","n":"Bacon and cabbage","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Irish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Bacon and cabbage is a dish especially associated with Ireland. The dish consists of sliced back bacon boiled with cabbage served with potatoes. Smoked bacon is sometimes used. The dish is served with the bacon sliced, and with some of the boiling juices added. Another common accompaniment to the dish is white sauce, which consists of flour, butter and milk, sometimes with a flavouring of some sort (often parsley)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bacon-and-cabbage"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bacon_and_cabbage"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Irish cuisine","cuisine/irish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Savoy cabbage","ingredient/savoy-cabbage"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Irish American Mom","ref":"site/irishamericanmom-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"irishamericanmom.com","note":"Irish-born cook living in the US sharing traditional Irish recipes.","url":"https://www.irishamericanmom.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Irish cuisine","links":[["Adare Manor","dish/adare-manor"],["Aimsir","dish/aimsir"],["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Crumble","dish/crumble"],["Eipic (restaurant)","dish/eipic-restaurant"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["L'Ecrivain","dish/l-ecrivain"],["Leo's Tavern","dish/leo-s-tavern"],["Loam (restaurant)","dish/loam-restaurant"],["Mews (restaurant)","dish/mews-restaurant"],["Ox (Belfast restaurant)","dish/ox-belfast-restaurant"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Restaurant Chestnut","dish/restaurant-chestnut"],["Sausage roll","dish/sausage-roll"],["The Muddlers Club","dish/the-muddlers-club"],["Timoleague Brown Pudding","dish/timoleague-brown-pudding"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ea/Bacon_and_cabbage.jpg/500px-Bacon_and_cabbage.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Miss Ayumi","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bacon_and_cabbage.jpg"}},"dish/bombolone":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bombolone","n":"Bombolone","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Bombolone is an Italian filled doughnut (similar to Berliner and pączek), eaten as a snack food and dessert. The pastry's name is etymologically related to bomba (lit. 'bomb'), and the same type of pastry is also called bomba (pl.: bombe) in some regions of Italy."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bombolone"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombolone"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba","dish/antica-pizzeria-port-alba"],["Antico Pizza","dish/antico-pizza"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["ASK Italian","dish/ask-italian"],["Asti (restaurant)","dish/asti-restaurant"],["Ava Gene's","dish/ava-gene-s"],["Bamonte's","dish/bamonte-s"],["Bar del Corso","dish/bar-del-corso"],["Barbetta","dish/barbetta"],["Barbuto (restaurant)","dish/barb